{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"b5846eae7879a0289e577bf5c3019cf394792c01282846305c2cfad757fea555","digest":{"component_or_area":"op-cert service configuration","key_entities":["REBAR_OPCERT_PRIVATE_KEY","OpcertServiceConfig.from_env","_private_key_env","src/rebar/opcert_service/config.py","compose_signer","keyprov._validate_key_file","workspace._git","os.environ.pop","tests/unit/test_opcert_privkey_env_pop_932d.py","infra/compose/docker-compose.yml","scripts/gen_env_registry.py"],"problem_keywords":["credential hygiene","environment variable leakage","inline PEM","op-cert","subprocess inheritance","secret exposure"],"propositions":["REBAR_OPCERT_PRIVATE_KEY is read from os.environ in _private_key_env but never removed, leaving the raw inline PEM in the process environment after config load","Child processes spawned after config load (ssh-keygen, git) inherit the unset inline PEM from os.environ because they receive no explicit env parameter","The inline PEM variable must be popped from os.environ immediately after being captured in _private_key_env to prevent exposure to subprocesses and environment dumps","compose_signer reads cfg.private_key directly and never touches the environment, so popping the variable at config read time does not break downstream callers","OpcertServiceConfig.from_env is called exactly once at module scope in app.py and the container runs without reload or worker modes, establishing a consume-once contract"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787482008266837001,"uuid":"12a14956-8744-4f59-9582-14eb3a0d209d"}